{# WHAT IS INSTALLED — the screen the front door used to be.

   `/` is the organization dashboard now, and what used to answer there is
   here: what this installation runs, at what version, which areas run it, and
   whether any of it needs attention. It is the one screen in the product that
   is about the SOFTWARE rather than about the work.

   NOTHING ON IT IS PER-AREA CONFIGURATION, which is what the hint at the
   bottom says: turning a module on for one area is the area's own business,
   and what that module then does is that module's Configure page.

   TWO FIGURES AND TWO COLUMNS STATE THEIR OWN ABSENCE on an ordinary
   installation, and that is the honest reading rather than a gap. Whether a
   package is BEHIND needs a release feed to compare against and when the
   installation last DEPLOYED needs whatever deployed it to have said so;
   neither is a thing a running application can read about itself, and a
   screen that filled them in would be guessing on the one page whose whole
   job is not to. #}
{% extends '@Shell/settings/_section.html.twig' %}

{% block shell_page %}
    {{ include('@Shell/settings/_figures.html.twig', {figures: settings.installationFigures}, with_context: false) }}

    <h2 class="zone">What is installed</h2>

    <div class="c">
        <span class="tab">What is installed<span class="src">&middot; the core and every package beside it, with the version this installation runs</span></span>
        <a class="more" href="{{ modulesUrl }}">Modules &rarr;</a>
        <table class="tbl">
            <tr>
                <th>package</th>
                <th>what it is</th>
                <th>installed</th>
                <th>released</th>
                <th>state</th>
            </tr>
            {%- for package in settings.packages -%}
                <tr>
                    <td><b>{{ package.name }}</b></td>
                    <td>{{ package.line ?? '—' }}</td>
                    <td class="mono">{{ package.version }}</td>
                    {# NOTHING TO COMPARE AGAINST. An installation reads its own
                       vendor directory and no index of releases, so the two
                       columns the design draws beside the version are drawn and
                       left honestly empty — the card's caption below says why,
                       once, rather than each row saying it five times. #}
                    <td class="mono fog">—</td>
                    <td class="fog">—</td>
                </tr>
            {%- endfor -%}
        </table>
        <p class="use">Read from composer at render time, so this is what the installation
            actually has. What has been RELEASED is not read from anywhere: nothing here
            subscribes to a release feed, so no row can say it is behind.</p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="zone">What runs where</h2>

    <div class="c">
        <span class="tab">Modules per area<span class="src">&middot;
            {{ settings.matrix.rows|length }} area{{ settings.matrix.rows|length == 1 ? '' : 's' }} &middot;
            {{ settings.matrix.columns|length }} module{{ settings.matrix.columns|length == 1 ? '' : 's' }} &middot;
            {{ settings.matrix.liveAreas }} running</span></span>
        {{ include('@Shell/settings/_matrix.html.twig', {matrix: settings.matrix}, with_context: false) }}
    </div>

    <h2 class="zone">Health</h2>

    <div class="c">
        <span class="tab">Health<span class="src">&middot;
            {%- if settings.checks is empty %} nothing installed here publishes a check yet
            {%- else %} {{ settings.checks|length }} check{{ settings.checks|length == 1 ? '' : 's' }} &middot;
                {{ settings.checksPassed }} pass
                {%- if settings.checksPassed < settings.checks|length %} &middot;
                    {{ settings.checks|length - settings.checksPassed }} to check
                {%- endif -%}
            {%- endif -%}
        </span></span>
        {%- for check in settings.checks -%}
            <div class="rln">
                <span><span class="chip {{ check.passed ? 'ok' : 'warn' }}">{{ check.passed ? 'pass' : 'check' }}</span>
                    <b>{{ check.title }}</b></span>
                {%- if check.detail %}<span class="mono fog">{{ check.detail }}</span>{% endif -%}
            </div>
        {%- else -%}
            <p class="use">A check arrives with whatever can answer it — the core answers for
                what it keeps, and a module answers for its own. Nothing installed here
                publishes one yet, which is a reading and not a failure.</p>
        {%- endfor -%}
    </div>

    {{ include('@Shell/_page_hint.html.twig', {
        lead: 'Nothing on this page is per-area configuration.',
        say: 'It states what this installation is. Turning a module on or off for one area is that area’s own business, and what the module then does is its own Configure page.',
    }, with_context: false) }}
{% endblock %}
